                    {
                        "form_id": "4133cee3-edd4-4a6c-ab83-96f66ed638e7",
                        "entry_id": "8d6b86e7-f7be-38f9-9f46-6260832780f2",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "dispraised"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "3cd6e052-e22b-490b-902a-e96f1e0f1572",
                        "entry_id": "8d6b86e7-f7be-38f9-9f46-6260832780f2",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "dispraised"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7fa90536-5e98-3a87-bb44-6341112a5525",
                        "entry_id": "8d6b86e7-f7be-38f9-9f46-6260832780f2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To notice with disapprobation or some degree of censure; to disparage, to criticize."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "918cfe1f-0f92-4094-9b2e-8655a5dcb550",
                                "sense_id": "7fa90536-5e98-3a87-bb44-6341112a5525",
                                "text": "They spake agaynst it, and dispraysed it, raylinge on it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b2e6d0d-de1c-4867-87e0-d286b193cb65",
                                "sense_id": "7fa90536-5e98-3a87-bb44-6341112a5525",
                                "text": "Although I dispraise not the defence of just immunities, yet love my peace better, if that were all."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d83823b2-d2ee-4676-83c2-87b8f5dde4e8",
                                "sense_id": "7fa90536-5e98-3a87-bb44-6341112a5525",
                                "text": "\"What,\" thought Edward, \"the poet says in praise of one beauty, I say in dispraise of another: 'Her eyes, like suns, the rash beholder strike, But, like the sun, they shine on all alike.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7eb9b8d9-b22a-479d-9994-33c60d2284ef",
                                "sense_id": "7fa90536-5e98-3a87-bb44-6341112a5525",
                                "text": "He became familiar with that habit of mind which dispraises what it most envies and admires: with that habit of mind which desires only what it cannot have."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e0afb7d-3b1d-4a00-ba2e-3a2cf680456f",
                                "sense_id": "7fa90536-5e98-3a87-bb44-6341112a5525",
                                "text": "Mira could not find a single article dispraising him."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
